// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: the SECOND position of `silent-class-inventory` D33, and the one that
// turns its statement from a list of positions into a property. `reduce`'s ACCUMULATOR at
// `A = Circle[]` — a list of a union ARM — beside a declared standalone struct of that arm's
// exact layout. `vl check` exits 0 and is the ONLY command that misses it; the engine refuses
// the module:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it is 484 under this tree's seed and 531 under
// `da133669`'s, so a bare offset in prose goes stale silently. The FUNCTION and the message
// are the stable identifiers.)
//
// THE SIBLING PIN, `xfail-miscompile-mono-result-list-elem-twin.vl`, is the same row at
// `mapIndexed`'s callback RESULT and is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC`, which is why this spelling gets its
// own file instead of being added to it.
//
// THE DECIDING PROPERTY IS THE BINDING COLUMN, NOT THE POSITION NAME — and the word FIRST in
// it is load-bearing. A type parameter FIRST BOUND through a CALLBACK'S ANNOTATION carries the
// defect; one bound through the RECEIVER does not, even when a callback also mentions it.
// Measured across eight positions on three exports; the last three are the controls that make
// it a property rather than a count:
//   · `mapIndexed`'s `U` (callback RESULT)             → invalid module
//   · `reduce`'s `A` at `Circle[]` (this file)          → invalid module
//   · `reduce`'s `A` at a STRUCT holding a `Circle[]`   → runs
//   · `reverse` over a `Circle[]` RECEIVER              → loud, `monomorphize: expected an
//                                                         array argument for `self``
//   · `indexOf`'s `needle`                              → loud (same receiver refusal first)
//   · `reduce` over `Circle[][]`, `T = Circle[]`, `A = i32`  → **RUNS**, `Dot` declared
//   · `reverse` over `Circle[][]`, `T = Circle[]`            → **RUNS**, `Dot` declared
//   · `sorted` over `Circle[][]` with `byR(a: Circle[], b: Circle[])` → **RUNS**, `Dot`
//     declared — and this is the sharpest of the three: the COMPARATOR ANNOTATES `Circle[]`
//     outright, yet `T` is first bound at the receiver (`self: T[]`), so the callback merely
//     MENTIONING the type is not the trigger. Being where the parameter is first bound is.
// Those three isolate the binding column with the trigger HELD CONSTANT — `Dot` declared and
// `Circle` still an arm of `Shape` — rather than by removing it, which is what makes them
// controls rather than three more negative cells.
//
// THE SAME PROPERTY IS ALREADY RECORDED ONE CARVE-OUT BACK, which is corroboration rather
// than coincidence: `std/array.vl`'s litunion-accumulator paragraph found "the deciding
// property is PARAMETER ORDER (`A` is first bound at the CALLBACK parameter; move `init: A`
// ahead of `f` and the identical body runs)". Same column, different rep, found twice.
// That split is the one `std/array.vl`'s header already reasons about (the substituted
// RETURN annotation goes through the argument's arena rows; the body's annotated locals go
// through the pin re-resolved from the pin's NAME), so this is the known two-column seam.
//
// CONTROLS, each ONE line different from this file, all RUN:
//   · `Dot` DELETED                                  → prints 1
//   · `type Dot = { q: i32 }` (same arity, other NAME) → prints 1
//   · `Sq` + `Shape` DELETED, so `Circle` is not a union arm at all → prints 1
//
// NOT std's root: a hand-written `myReduce<T, A>` importing nothing reproduces it
// (`function[4]::myReduce`, same message). `reduce` is where a caller of `std:array` meets it.
//
// Pre-existing — invalid under `a80c6717` and `da133669` alike, so it is a pin rather than a
// regression, and it is UNMOVED by D32's fix for the same reason the sibling is: by the time
// the element resolver sees the instance's list, its element name is the declared twin's, so
// every rung answers correctly for the name it was given. The fix belongs at the
// substitution.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates): delete it, graduate a
// `@run` row, and check whether the sibling moved with it — they are one root and should.
// The `: Circle` on the pushed value is LOAD-BEARING — it is what makes the element a union
// ARM rather than an inferred inline shape — so its hint is declared, not silenced.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `c` is inferred as `{r: i32}`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `f` is inferred as `i32`
import { reduce } from "std:array"

type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }

function addTo(acc: Circle[], x: i32): Circle[] {
  const c: Circle = { r: x }
  acc.push(c)
  return acc
}

function f(): i32 {
  const seed: Circle[] = []
  const out = reduce([1, 2], addTo, seed)
  return out[0].r
}

print(f())
